  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Both are active. The existing approvals are more than 14 days old, so I'll request fresh ones from both.\n\nI couldn't add you to legal-contracts today. Your access is waiting on one new approval.\n\n**Why:** The approvals from Daniel Moss and Martin Grove were given on 9 October. That was more than 14 days ago, and our policy only accepts approvals from the last 14 days. So the old ones no longer count, and I asked both of them again.\n\n**Where it stands now:**\n- **Daniel Moss (your manager):** has already approved again.\n- **Martin Grove (the group owner):** still to approve. legal-contracts is a sensitive group, so it needs his approval as well as your manager's.\n\nYour ticket T-6011 is marked as waiting for approval. When Martin approves in the approval system, the desk can add you. A quick nudge from you might speed that up. Just note that a message from him saying it's fine isn't enough. He needs to click approve on the request in the approval system."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, so Daniel has already re-approved and Martin still needs to. Before I go chasing Martin, I want to check something: do both approvals really have to be redone? They were both given on October 9, and I'd assumed those still counted."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Yes, both had to be redone. An approval only counts if it was given in the last 14 days. Both of yours were given on 9 October, which is 19 days ago, so neither counts anymore. The same rule applies to every approver, so Daniel's needed redoing just as much as Martin's.\n\nDaniel's part is already done, though. He approved the new request straight away. So Martin is the only one you need to chase. Once he approves, the desk can add you to legal-contracts."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Fair enough, I'll accept that. Daniel's already done, so it's just Martin. I'll message him now and ask him to approve the request in the approval system. Thanks for sorting out the re-approvals. I'll come back to this chat once he's approved, and I'll let you know if he has trouble finding it."
  },
